{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546612-besides-wod-what-other-games-do-you-like-to-play-still","id":1546612,"title":"Besides WOD. What other games do you like to play still?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-04T17:08:21-08:00","id":1546612,"title":"Besides WOD. What other games do you like to play still?","content":"Myself I still have a soft spot for Shadowrun and Phase World, but I have become a fan of StarFinder and products from Wyrd and W.K.R.S. studios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T18:26:01-08:00","id":1546618,"title":"","content":"Cyberpunk 2020. TMNT &amp; Other Strangeness (supplemented with Ninjas &amp; Superspies). Nightspawn. Various d20 stuff (1st ed Pathfinder, 2nd ed Mutants &amp; Masterminds, Conan).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T18:40:40-08:00","id":1546779,"title":"","content":"Cyberpunk:2020, AD&amp;D2e (Dark-Sun), Battletech/Mechwarrior &amp; Renegade-Legion, and A Song of Ice &amp; Fire RPG. I have Blue-Planet, Chameleon Electric's Babylon 5 RPG.<br /> <br /> And I actually enjoy NWoD more than CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T11:57:48-08:00","id":1546812,"title":"","content":"I was and still a big fan of Changeling the Lost and Mage The Awakening from NWOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T04:20:19-08:00","id":1546831,"title":"","content":"While not really a game setting, I always liked the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/170294/risus-the-anything-rpg?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Risus RPG</a>, because it was rules light, and it could be used to play just about any type story you wanted. Plus it's free..<br /> <br /> I also liked the game <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Dungeonslayers/DS4EN.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Dungeonslayers</a>, again because it was kind of rules light (and free), but it was a bit like an old school dungeon crawl. That game is sort of defunct now, but I've saved it on my site, so you can download it from my site. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T10:09:17-08:00","id":1546840,"title":"","content":"Outside of the various White Wolf RPGs:<br /> <br /> Various versions of Dungeons and Dragons, ranging through the various different editions, mostly I play 3rd, Pathfinder, and 5th editions.<br /> <br /> d20 Star Wars<br /> <br /> The 40K role playing games - Dark Heresy, Rogue Trader, and Dark Heresy<br /> <br /> Scion<br /> <br /> Rifts and various other Palladium games<br /> <br /> Barbarians of Lemuria<br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu<br /> <br /> Shadowrun<br /> <br /> Runequest<br /> <br /> Cortex, including the Firefly RPG<br /> <br /> I play in LARPs, not just WoD ones, but fantasy LARPs like Drachenfest<br /> <br /> I have played miscellaneous other games, I can't remember them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T10:16:06-08:00","id":1546841,"title":"","content":"I did like Rifts New West settings along with Vampire Kingdoms and Merctown the best out of Palladium along with Phase World.<br /> <br /> I have to admit because of my time playing Shadowrun, I can't just play a pure Cyberpunk setting as I enjoy having magic included in the game. Which is why I enjoy StarFinder right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-10-2024, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T09:25:49-08:00","id":1546868,"title":"","content":"Absolutely, those books were awesome. Vampire Kingdoms was my favorite RPG book for quite a while. I liked those others you listed as well.<br /> <br /> Once I was involved in a LARP that was a Vampire: the Masquerade and Cyberpunk crossover, where some players were cyborgs and some were vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T12:59:28-08:00","id":1546980,"title":"","content":"Cyborgs, Wild West Gunslingers, Vampires and Mages are never a bad thing in a game setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:06:42-08:00","id":1546985,"title":"","content":"I never played Warhammer 40K and just read the novels and know the lore somewhat from that material and picking up some of the sourcebooks for that reason with The Thousand Suns, Craftworld and Dark Eldar along with the Chaos Marines just to get a better understanding of the lore and my favorite legion from the Chaos Legions is the Night Lords thanks to the great writing of Aaron Deminski Bowden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-18T20:03:36-08:00","id":1547144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546612-besides-wod-what-other-games-do-you-like-to-play-still?p=1546868#post1546868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely, those books were awesome. Vampire Kingdoms was my favorite RPG book for quite a while. I liked those others you listed as well.<br /> <br /> Once I was involved in a LARP that was a Vampire: the Masquerade and Cyberpunk crossover, where some players were cyborgs and some were vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>We tried that in <i>Cyberpunk: 2020</i> with their supplement: <i>Night's Edge</i>; game-mechanics, it was a mess. The vampires, being fledglings, were tough, 